<div class='wrap'>
  <header>
    <div>
      <h1>American Express (AXP) Historical Stock Performance Report: 1972–2026</h1>
      <div class='subtitle'>A dataset-driven review of over five decades of daily AXP trading history, focused on long-horizon price compounding, drawdowns, volatility, and dividends.</div>
    </div>
    <div class='meta' id='metaBox'>Loading data…</div>
  </header>

  <section class='grid'>
    <div class='card' style='grid-column: span 12;'>
      <div class='hd'>KPI Dashboard (Close-based)</div>
      <div class='bd'>
        <div class='kpis' id='kpiGrid'></div>
        <p class='small'><span class='warn'>Data integrity note:</span> This report uses only values computed directly from the provided dataset. The dataset documentation indicates prices appear adjusted for splits and dividends; therefore the KPI labeled “Cumulative Price Return” and “CAGR (Close)” are computed from the dataset’s <code>Close</code> series, and the dividend KPI is a separate sum of <code>Dividends</code>. A fully specified reinvested total-return series is not uniquely computable from the dataset alone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class='row'>
      <div class='card'>
        <div class='hd'>Executive Overview</div>
        <div class='bd'>
          <p id='execSummary'>Loading…</p>
          <div class='callout' style='margin-top: 12px;' id='atlAthBox'></div>
          <ul id='insightsList'></ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <div class='hd'>Risk Callouts (Close-based Drawdowns)</div>
        <div class='bd'>
          <p>Historically important stress windows quantified using closing prices:</p>
          <ul id='riskCallouts'></ul>
          <p class='small'>Max drawdown is computed as the minimum of (price / running-peak − 1).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class='card'>
      <div class='hd'>Long-Term Price Trend Analysis (Centerpiece)</div>
      <div class='bd'>
        <div class='toolbar' style='margin-bottom:10px;'>
          <button id='scaleLin' class='btn active'>Linear scale</button>
          <button id='scaleLog' class='btn'>Log scale</button>
          <span class='note'>Log scale makes multi-decade compounding comparable.</span>
        </div>
        <svg id='priceChart' class='svgbox' viewBox='0 0 1000 340' preserveAspectRatio='none'></svg>
        <p class='small'>Daily <code>Close</code> series. Use log scale to interpret growth rates; linear scale emphasizes absolute price changes in later years.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class='row'>
      <div class='card'>
        <div class='hd'>Volatility & Risk Assessment</div>
        <div class='bd'>
          <svg id='ddChart' class='svgbox tall' viewBox='0 0 1000 260' preserveAspectRatio='none'></svg>
          <p class='small' id='ddCaption'>Loading…</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <div class='hd'>Worst Drawdown Episodes (Top 10)</div>
        <div class='bd'>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Drawdown</th><th>Peak Date</th><th class='num'>Peak Close</th><th>Trough Date</th><th class='num'>Trough Close</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id='worstDdRows'></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class='card'>
      <div class='hd'>Trading Volume Analysis</div>
      <div class='bd'>
        <svg id='volChart' class='svgbox tall' viewBox='0 0 1000 260' preserveAspectRatio='none'></svg>
        <p class='small' id='volNote'>Loading…</p>
        <div class='card' style='margin-top:12px; box-shadow:none;'>
          <div class='hd'>Largest Volume Days (Top 12)</div>
          <div class='bd'>
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th class='num'>Volume</th><th class='num'>Close</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody id='topVolRows'></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class='row'>
      <div class='card'>
        <div class='hd'>Dividend History & Stock Splits</div>
        <div class='bd'>
          <p id='divSummary'>Loading…</p>
          <div class='callout' style='margin-top:10px;' id='divBox'></div>
          <h3 style='margin: 14px 0 0; font-size:14px;'>Stock Splits (dataset events)</h3>
          <table style='margin-top:8px;'>
            <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th class='num'>Split Ratio</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id='splitRows'></tbody>
          </table>
          <p class='small'>This section reports dividend cash distributions and split events as recorded. It does not assume dividend reinvestment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <div class='hd'>Annual Returns (Close-to-Close)</div>
        <div class='bd'>
          <svg id='annRetChart' class='svgbox tall' viewBox='0 0 1000 260' preserveAspectRatio='none'></svg>
          <p class='small' id='annCaption'>Loading…</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class='card'>
      <div class='hd'>Decade-by-Decade Performance Comparison</div>
      <div class='bd'>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Period</th><th class='num'>Start</th><th class='num'>End</th><th class='num'>Start Close</th><th class='num'>End Close</th>
              <th class='num'>Price Return</th><th class='num'>CAGR</th><th class='num'>Ann. Vol</th><th class='num'>Max DD</th><th class='num'>Dividends (Sum)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id='decadeRows'></tbody>
        </table>
        <p class='small'>Volatility is annualized from daily returns (×√252). Max drawdown is computed within each period from closes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class='footer'>
    <div class='card'>
      <div class='hd'>Methodology & Limitations</div>
      <div class='bd'>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Price series:</b> all trend/return/volatility/drawdown metrics use the dataset’s daily <code>Close</code> values.</li>
          <li><b>Volatility:</b> population stdev of daily returns annualized by √252.</li>
          <li><b>Dividends:</b> “Total Dividends Paid” is the simple sum of <code>Dividends</code>.</li>
          <li><b>Total return:</b> a reinvested total-return series cannot be uniquely derived from this dataset alone.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class='small' id='buildStamp'></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

